---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import JsonFlattenTool from '../../components/JsonFlattenTool.jsx';
---
<ToolLayout title="JSON Flatten / Unflatten" description="Convert nested JSON into flat dot-notation keys, or rebuild nested JSON from flat keys.">
  <JsonFlattenTool client:load slot="tool" />
  <h2>When this is useful</h2>
  <p>Flat key-value structures are easier to use in CSV exports, environment variables, or simple key-based storage systems. Unflatten reverses the process to restore the original nested shape.</p>

  <h2>Common JSON Flatten Mistakes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Losing array structure information</strong> when flattening, if the flattening scheme doesn't clearly distinguish array indices from object keys.</li>
    <li><strong>Not verifying round-trip accuracy</strong> — flatten then unflatten should reproduce the original structure exactly; test this before relying on it for critical data.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When to Use This JSON Flatten Tool</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Preparing nested JSON for export to a flat CSV format</li>
    <li>Converting nested config into flat environment variable names</li>
    <li>Rebuilding a nested object structure from flat key-value storage</li>
  </ul>
</ToolLayout>
